<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">My Tho</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mỹ Tho</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">My Tho is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> delta of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, capital of Tien Giang province, on the northern branch of the Mekong. It was founded in the late 17th century by Ming loyalist refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under Duong Ngan Dich, settled there with the permission of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a>, and grew into a major market town of the delta. In 1785 the Tay Son destroyed a Siamese army nearby at Rach Gam–Xoai Mut.</p></div>
